window.CET4_EE_TEMPLATES = ["Undetermined. Survived 100,000 steps and then 2,000,000 steps without a collision, and no local configuration repeat was found within that window. It may halt later, or never.","Nonhalting (certified). The pair repeats as a unit -- same states, same gap, tape shifted by the same amount for both heads -- so the distance between them never changes and a collision is impossible.","Nonhalting (certified). One agent loops inside a fixed band while the other moves away monotonically, so the two heads can never share a cell.","Nonhalting (certified). Both agents loop inside disjoint fixed bands, so the two heads can never share a cell.","Likely nonhalting, unproven. Both heads drift, at different rates. Neither the trailing head catching the leading one nor the reverse can be ruled out from local repeats, so this is not certified.","Halting. A collision was witnessed by direct simulation, so both the halt and the step count are proven.","Undetermined. A local configuration appeared to repeat, but the repeat fails the exact tape comparison, so it does not continue forever and no glide follows from it. It may halt.","Undetermined. Both heads look periodic within 65 cells and the gap between them repeats, but the region actually swept in between does not repeat exactly, so it is a pseudo-glide rather than a glide. It may halt."];
